{"id":25201398929354,"type":"album","name":"Aesthethica","artist":"Liturgy","year":2011,"weight":10,"info":{"cover":"https://dn710605.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-216dc68b-c7db-4c5f-b054-753d6d3fd1d1/mbid-216dc68b-c7db-4c5f-b054-753d6d3fd1d1-12911239802.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":12,"country":"US","scaruffi":7.5,"yt":"xm8obBcg7Ts","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/4qutu7PdlUa7ZdYzsXI1EW","youtube":"https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_lByFWx67JYDndVeYTR0QBAsPekUcwZnN8","bandcamp":"https://liturgy.bandcamp.com/album/aesthethica"},"desc":"Brooklyn based Liturgy is Hunter Hunt Hendrix, Greg Fox, Tyler Dusenbury, and Bernard Gann. Aesthethica, their second album and third release, shows the band exploring, in greater depth, themes initially touched on by their critically acclaimed debut album, Renihilation. The band used every instrument, literal or figurative, to produce meaning and intensity, disregarding the genre boundaries of black metal, hardcore and experimental music. On Renihilation, Liturgy made use of simple song structures, and concentrated on sustaining a blindingly high intensity level from start to finish. Aesthethica, a more controlled and polyvalent effort, finds the band operating at multiple levels and ."},"artist_ref":{"id":73076788306641,"name":"Liturgy","info":{"img":null}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":170438788671559,"type":"genre","name":"Black Metal","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":313,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":125057452333169,"type":"genre","name":"Math Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":299,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":107889004937350,"type":"genre","name":"EBM","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":237,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":169159335096911,"type":"genre","name":"Avant-Garde Metal","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":228,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":23184402430853,"type":"genre","name":"Electro-Industrial","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":213,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":844